Hochul insisted she’s helping, not hurting, public school students by opting into the federal scholarship program.

“Every parent wants their child to have a great education and the best possible chance to succeed. That’s what guides my decisions as Governor.

“New York’s public schools are the backbone of communities across this state. That’s why I’ve made historic investments in public education, increasing school funding by more than $10 billion and fully funding Foundation Aid for the first time.”
